import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Ultra mode"
  eyebrow="Capabilities"
  description="Enable proactive multi-agent delegation for any Roder model with /ultra or the app-server control plane."
  prev={{ href: "/docs/agent-swarm/", title: "Agent swarm" }}
  next={{ href: "/docs/agent-control/", title: "Agent control" }}
>
  <p>
    Ultra mode turns on proactive multi-agent delegation for the current Roder thread.
    It is a runtime mode, so it works with any provider and model that can use Roder's
    agent-control tools. The visible transcript stays exactly as typed; Roder injects the
    delegation policy into the turn's developer instructions before the provider call.
  </p>

  <p>
    Use Ultra when the task benefits from parallel search, review, implementation, or
    verification. It does not relax sandboxing, policy mode, approval handling, tool
    allowlists, workspace boundaries, or credential access.
  </p>

  <h2>TUI commands</h2>
  <pre><code>/ultra
/ultra on
/ultra off
/ultra status
/ultra audit this change with parallel reviewers</code></pre>

  <ul>
    <li><code>/ultra</code> toggles persistent Ultra mode for the thread.</li>
    <li><code>/ultra on</code> and <code>/ultra off</code> force the persistent state.</li>
    <li><code>/ultra status</code> reports whether Ultra mode is active.</li>
    <li><code>/ultra &lt;prompt&gt;</code> runs one Ultra task without changing the persistent toggle.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>
    When persistent Ultra mode is enabled, the composer title includes
    <strong>Ultra</strong>. If agent-swarm mode is also enabled, the label includes both
    modes.
  </p>

  <h2>How it relates to Sol and Terra Ultra effort</h2>
  <p>
    Codex Sol and Terra still expose <code>ultra</code> as a reasoning effort. Selecting
    that effort maps to the provider's <code>max</code> wire effort and enables proactive
    delegation. Ultra mode is separate: it enables the same proactive delegation policy
    without changing reasoning effort, and it works for models that do not advertise an
    Ultra effort.
  </p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>State</th>
        <th>Effect</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>/ultra on</code></td>
        <td>Proactive multi-agent policy for the active model.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Sol or Terra with <code>ultra</code> effort</td>
        <td>Provider <code>max</code> effort plus proactive multi-agent policy.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Sol or Terra at a lower effort, Ultra mode off</td>
        <td>Teammates remain explicit-request-only.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Other models with Ultra mode off</td>
        <td>No proactive multi-agent policy is injected.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>App-server controls</h2>
  <p>
    Clients can drive the same state with <code>thread/set_ultra_mode</code>. Passing a
    <code>threadId</code> stores a thread override; omitting it changes the runtime-global
    default. <code>settings/get</code> exposes the global <code>ultraMode</code> setting,
    and the notification stream emits <code>ultra/modeChanged</code> when the mode changes.
  </p>

  <pre><code>{`{
  "method": "thread/set_ultra_mode",
  "params": {
    "threadId": "thread-123",
    "enabled": true,
    "trigger": "manual"
  }
}`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Subagents and swarm work</h2>
  <p>
    Ultra mode uses the existing <a href="/docs/agent-control/">agent-control</a> tools
    for open-ended teammate work. It also composes with
    <a href="/docs/agent-swarm/">agent-swarm mode</a>, which nudges the model toward the
    homogeneous <code>agent_swarm</code> fanout tool for many similarly shaped items.
  </p>

  <p>
    Spawned <code>task</code> and <code>agent_swarm</code> children inherit the parent
    thread's live provider and model unless an explicit compatible override is supplied.
    Large fanouts can request a higher lane <code>max_concurrent</code>, still bounded by
    dispatcher caps and policy.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
